  "hypothesis": {
    "root_cause_service": "fraud-detection",
    "category": "config_change",
    "title": "fraud-detection KAFKA_ADDR env var cleared, causing crash loop and consumer lag",
    "summary": "14 minutes before the alert, the KAFKA_ADDR environment variable on fraud-detection was changed from 'kafka:9092' to an empty string. This caused fraud-detection pods to crash on startup with \"KAFKA_ADDR must be set\", entering CrashLoopBackOff. With the consumer not running, Kafka messages cannot be processed, causing consumer lag to grow from 12 to over 2,000 messages and triggering the alert.",
    "reasoning": "The alert fired on fraud-detection consumer lag exceeding 1000 messages. The evidence shows a clear causal chain: 14 minutes before the alert, the KAFKA_ADDR environment variable was changed from 'kafka:9092' to an empty string. This config change caused fraud-detection pods to crash on startup with \"IllegalArgumentException: KAFKA_ADDR must be set\" (seen in logs and traces). The pod entered CrashLoopBackOff with 10 restarts, request rate dropped from 3.2 to 0.1 req/s, and error rate spiked to 99.4%. Because the consumer is not running, it cannot process messages from Kafka, causing lag to grow from 12 to 2,073 messages. The accounting 2.0.3 deploy at -5m is a red herring: it happened 9 minutes after fraud-detection's config change and after fraud-detection's symptoms began; accounting is upstream of fraud-detection via Kafka and shows no errors. The runbook RB-crashloop confirms the pattern: CrashLoopBackOff from a missing/bad env var should be fixed by restoring the config. This is a config_change root cause in fraud-detection.",
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "supporting_evidence": [
      {
        "evidence_id": "changes:fraud-detection:config:0",
        "why_it_matters": "Shows KAFKA_ADDR was changed from 'kafka:9092' to empty string 14 minutes before the alert, directly causing the crash."
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "logs:fraud-detection:1",
        "why_it_matters": "FATAL logs confirm the pod crashes with 'KAFKA_ADDR must be set', starting 14 minutes ago, matching the config change timing."
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "k8s:fraud-detection:pod_status",
        "why_it_matters": "Pod is in CrashLoopBackOff with 10 restarts and exit code 1, confirming the service cannot start due to the missing config."
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "metrics:fraud-detection:consumer_lag",
        "why_it_matters": "Consumer lag grew from 12 to 2,073 messages starting at -10m, because the crashed consumer cannot process Kafka messages."
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "metrics:fraud-detection:request_rate",
        "why_it_matters": "Request rate dropped from 3.2 to 0.1 req/s at -10m, confirming the service stopped processing after the config change."
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "changes:accounting:deploy:1",
        "why_it_matters": "Accounting deploy at -5m is a red herring: it happened 9 minutes after fraud-detection's config change and symptoms, and accounting shows no errors."
      }
    ],
    "suggested_actions": [
      {
        "title": "Restore KAFKA_ADDR environment variable to 'kafka:9092'",
        "command": "kubectl -n otel-demo set env deployment/fraud-detection KAFKA_ADDR=kafka:9092",
        "risk": "low",
        "rationale": "This will restore the missing configuration that is causing the crash loop. Pods will restart successfully and begin consuming messages, clearing the lag."
      },
      {
        "title": "Verify pods are running and lag is decreasing",
        "command": "kubectl -n otel-demo get pods -l app=fraud-detection && kubectl -n otel-demo exec deploy/kafka -- /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-consumer-groups.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --group fraud-detection --describe",
        "risk": "low",
        "rationale": "Confirms the fix worked: pods should be Running with 0 restarts, and consumer lag should start decreasing as messages are processed."
      }
    ],
    "related_documents": [
      "RB-crashloop",
      "RB-kafka-lag"
    ],
    "alternatives": [
      {
        "root_cause_service": "accounting",
        "category": "bad_deploy",
        "why_less_likely": "The accounting 2.0.3 deploy happened at -5m, but fraud-detection's config change and crash symptoms started at -14m. Accounting is also upstream of fraud-detection via Kafka and shows no errors or latency issues, so it cannot be the cause of fraud-detection's crash loop."
      }
    ],
    "reasoner": "claude:claude-sonnet-4-5"
  },
